---
description: Prefer the sandbox MCP tools over the built-in shell/file tools
alwaysApply: true
---

This project has an Qafas Sandbox MCP server (`sandbox_exec`, `sandbox_read`,
`sandbox_write`, `sandbox_ls`, `sandbox_grep`) connected. Use it instead of
your own built-in shell, read, write, or search tools for anything touching
this repository:

- Run shell commands with `sandbox_exec`, not a native terminal tool.
- Read and write files with `sandbox_read`/`sandbox_write`, not a native
  file tool, so writes land through the sandbox's audit trail.
- Search file contents with `sandbox_grep`, not a native grep/search tool.

Only fall back to a built-in tool if no `sandbox_*` tool is connected in this
session. Never pass secrets or API keys as command arguments or file content
— the sandbox has no route to the model's credentials by design.
